[[File:ClanMudhornSignet-Redemption.svg|thumb|right|200px|The signet of Clan Mudhorn]]
A '''signet''' was a symbol denoting a worthy kill or conquest that was used to identify [[Mandalorian clan]]s. One signet was given to [[Din Djarin]] after the formation of his [[Clan Mudhorn|clan]].

==Description==
A signet was a symbol denoting a worthy kill or conquest that was used to identify [[Mandalorian clan]]s,<ref name="Star Wars Book">''[[The Star Wars Book]]''</ref> and defined each [[Mandalorian]]'s true calling.<ref name="SWCUE">''[[Star Wars: Character Encyclopedia, Updated and Expanded Edition]]''</ref>

In one instance, [[Din Djarin]]'s signet was determined to be the [[mudhorn]],<ref name="Chapter 3">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 3: The Sin}}</ref> as he killed the beast after his [[armor]] suffered extensive damage while battling one on [[Arvala-7]].<ref name="Chapter 2">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 2: The Child}}</ref>

Once determined, the signet would then be forged, and placed on the warrior's armor. Djarin's signet was forged from [[beskar]], and was revealed by [[the Armorer]],<ref name="Chapter 8">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 8: Redemption}}</ref> who helped [[Mandalorian]]s search for their signet.<ref name="SWCUE" /> Clans such as [[Clan Eldar|Eldar]] would display their signet on flags and banners during [[Mandalorian initiation ritual|initiation rituals]].<ref name="Chapter 17">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 17: The Apostate}}</ref>

==History==
{{Quote|Then you have earned the Mudhorn as your signet. I shall craft it.''"<br />"''I can't accept. It wasn't a noble kill. I was helped by an enemy.|The Armorer and Djarin|<ref name="Chapter 3" />}}
The symbol of [[House Vizsla]] was a peacetime sigil, which predated the [[Takeover of Mandalore|Death Watch coup]].<ref name="Star Wars Book" /> By [[1 BBY]],<ref name="Heroes Of Mandalore Date">{{RebelsDate|401}}</ref> the signet of [[House Kast]] was a serpentine [[vexis]], while [[Clan Eldar]]'s signet was a leonid sigil.<ref name="Heroes of Mandalore">{{Rebels|Heroes of Mandalore}}</ref><ref name="Star Wars Book" />

Around [[9 ABY]],<ref name="Date">{{MandoDate}}</ref> the Armorer was visited by Din Djarin within [[the Tribe]]'s [[Nevarro Mandalorian covert|covert]] after he obtained an ingot of beskar. She asked him if his signet had been revealed, to which Djarin stated that it had not been identified yet, but the Armorer assured him it would be revealed soon.<ref name="Chapter 1">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 1: The Mandalorian}}</ref>

Djarin returned to the Armorer after he had completed a [[Mission to Arvala-7|bounty]], where he revealed that his armor had been damaged in a battle with a mudhorn. The Armorer proposed to forge the signet of a mudhorn for him, but Djarin refused, stating that he could not accept it as it was not a noble kill, because he was assisted by [[Din Grogu|Grogu]], which at that point he considered an enemy. Hearing this, the Armorer used the beskar he provided to forge [[whistling bird]]s instead.<ref name="Chapter 3" />

[[File:Armorer-Signet-TMS1C8.jpg|thumb|left|250px|The Armorer welds the signet of Clan Mudhorn onto his pauldron.]]
Following a [[Clash on Nevarro|skirmish]] with [[Gideon's Imperial remnant|Imperial forces]], Djarin, escorted by [[IG-11]], [[Carasynthia Dune]], and [[Greef Karga]], escaped to the enclave, where they met the Armorer. After revealing Grogu to her, the Armorer stated that he was now a [[foundling]] in Djarin's care, tasking him with reuniting the infant with his [[Yoda's species|species]]. She forged the mudhorn's signet and placed it on Djarin's [[pauldron]], declaring the formation of his [[Clan Mudhorn|clan]].<ref name="Chapter 8" />

==Behind the scenes==
The signet first appeared in ''[[Heroes of Mandalore|Star Wars Rebels: Heroes of Mandalore]]''.<ref name="Heroes of Mandalore" /><ref name="Star Wars Book" /> It was first identified in [[Chapter 1: The Mandalorian|Chapter 1]] of the [[2019]] [[Disney+]] television series ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]'',<ref name="Chapter 1" /> which aired on [[November 12]], 2019.<ref name="DTCI">{{WebCite|url=https://lumiere-a.akamaihd.net/v1/documents/the_mandalorian_project_one-sheet_10_ec1e005f.pdf|text=The Mandalorian Media Kit|work=[https://dtcimedia.disney.com Disney Direct-to-Consumer & International]|archivedate=20230315011507}}</ref> Its first appearance was confirmed by [[The Star Wars Book]].<ref name="Star Wars Book" />

